// toolbox/memory.cla: curated Memory Manager declarations (Inside
// Macintosh II, "The Memory Manager"), toolbox-cookbook phase. Register
// (OS) convention throughout -- bit 11 clear on every trap word below
// (trap & 0x0800 == 0), per the Ch13 trap-table reading rule. Safe to
// redeclare identically in user code (Ch13 dedup rule).
//
// Provenance: NewPtr/DisposePtr (0xA11E/0xA01F), NewHandle/DisposeHandle
// (0xA122/0xA023), SetHandleSize (0xA024), BlockMoveData (0xA22E) --
// proven verbatim against runtime/clarus/list.cla's ListNewPtr family
// (ListNewPtr/ListDisposePtr/ListNewHandle/ListDisposeHandle/
// ListSetHandleSize/ListBlockMoveData), already-shipped `reg`
// declarations with the same trap words. (This citation also named
// testsuite/toolbox/cases_gestalt.cla's TbNewPtr/TbDisposePtr until
// pack3-standardfile Task 5a deleted them; the Apple-interfaces
// re-verification below is the authoritative evidence regardless.)
// HLock/HUnlock (0xA029/0xA02A)
// proven verbatim against runtime/clarus/native.cla's NatHLock/
// NatHUnlock. GetHandleSize (0xA025) and MoreMasters (0xA036) were
// originally checked only against Retro68 multiversal/defs/MemoryMgr.yaml.
//
// Apple-interfaces re-verification (toolbox-cookbook phase, 2026-08-07):
// every trap word and register binding below is now confirmed directly
// against Apple's own Universal Interfaces 3.4
// (Retro68/InterfacesAndLibraries/Interfaces), the authoritative source --
// multiversal/defs/*.yaml is a third-party reconstruction of those same
// tables and is UNTRUSTED WHEN CITED ALONE: a citation it is the SOLE
// source for has never been checked against Apple at all. (The anecdote
// that used to justify this rule here -- that multiversal put Gestalt's
// response register in the wrong place -- was itself wrong, and
// pack3-standardfile Task 5a retired it: multiversal's `Out<A0>` was
// RIGHT, and our A1 reading came from taking `Gestalt.h`'s `#pragma
// parameter` line as the trap's contract when it describes the INLINE
// GLUE. The sharper rule that survives: decode the inline words -- a
// `TWOWORDINLINE` routine's second word is glue you must reproduce or
// route around. See toolbox/osutils.cla.) Any multiversal citation above
// should be read as secondary corroboration only, superseded by the
// citations below.
//
//   NewPtr        CIncludes/MacMemory.h:547 `#pragma parameter __A0
//                 NewPtr(__D0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:515 `_NewPtr:
//                 OPWORD $A11E`. byteCount in D0, ptr result in A0 --
//                 matches `reg` (no explicit ret: default result
//                 register for a ptr return is A0).
//   DisposePtr    CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1066 `#pragma parameter
//                 DisposePtr(__A0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:1209 OPWORD
//                 $A01F. p in A0, void result.
//   NewHandle     CIncludes/MacMemory.h:433 `#pragma parameter __A0
//                 NewHandle(__D0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:355 OPWORD
//                 $A122. byteCount in D0, ptr result in A0.
//   DisposeHandle CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1110 `#pragma parameter
//                 DisposeHandle(__A0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:1270 OPWORD
//                 $A023. h in A0, void result.
//   GetHandleSize CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1162 `#pragma parameter __D0
//                 InlineGetHandleSize(__A0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:1342
//                 OPWORD $A025 (Apple's real GetHandleSize is a full CFM
//                 call; InlineGetHandleSize is its 68k-direct inline
//                 twin, same trap word). h in A0, result in D0 -- matches
//                 `reg` exactly; the multiversal-only citation above is
//                 now redundant, not wrong.
//   SetHandleSize CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1125 `#pragma parameter
//                 SetHandleSize(__A0, __D0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:1291
//                 OPWORD $A024. h in A0, newSize in D0, matches `reg`
//                 positionally. The `memerr` clause is independently
//                 confirmed by AIncludes/Memory.a:402's own MemError():
//                 `TWOWORDINLINE(0x3EB8, 0x0220)` is literally `MOVE.W
//                 $0220,D0` -- MemError is nothing but a direct read of
//                 the low-memory MemErr global at $0220, exactly the
//                 mechanism `reg memerr` models. CIncludes/MacMemory.h's
//                 own comment above SetHandleSize/GetHandleSize confirms
//                 the shape too: "the traps actually return an error
//                 code in D0 ... the glue sets D0 to 0 if an error
//                 occurred" for the reads; SetHandleSize itself is a true
//                 void PROCEDURE trap (no result register at all in its
//                 pragma) whose real error status is MemErr-only, per
//                 Inside Macintosh's own Memory Manager chapter.
//   HLock         CIncludes/MacMemory.h:709 `#pragma parameter
//                 HLock(__A0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:731 OPWORD $A029.
//   HUnlock       CIncludes/MacMemory.h:724 `#pragma parameter
//                 HUnlock(__A0)`; AIncludes/MacMemory.a:751 OPWORD $A02A.
//   BlockMoveData CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1408 `#pragma parameter
//                 BlockMoveData(__A0, __A1, __D0)`; AIncludes/
//                 MacMemory.a:1658 OPWORD $A22E. srcPtr/destPtr/
//                 byteCount in A0/A1/D0 -- matches `reg`'s positional
//                 rule (two ptr params get A0 then A1 in declaration
//                 order, the one int param gets D0) exactly.
//   MoreMasters   CIncludes/MacMemory.h:1515 `MoreMasters(void)
//                 ONEWORDINLINE(0xA036)` (no register pragma -- zero
//                 args, void result); AIncludes/MacMemory.a:1781 OPWORD
//                 $A036.
//
// All ten trap words above are bit-11-clear (`trap & 0x0800 == 0`, per
// the Ch13 reading rule), confirming the `reg` convention this whole
// file uses.

external func NewPtr(byteCount: int): ptr = trap 0xA11E reg
external func DisposePtr(p: ptr) = trap 0xA01F reg
external func NewHandle(byteCount: int): ptr = trap 0xA122 reg
external func DisposeHandle(h: ptr) = trap 0xA023 reg
external func GetHandleSize(h: ptr): int = trap 0xA025 reg
external func SetHandleSize(h: ptr, newSize: int): int = trap 0xA024 reg memerr
external func HLock(h: ptr) = trap 0xA029 reg
external func HUnlock(h: ptr) = trap 0xA02A reg
external func BlockMoveData(srcPtr: ptr, destPtr: ptr, byteCount: int) = trap 0xA22E reg
external func MoreMasters() = trap 0xA036 reg
